 Citing ShellBuild beside ShellTypes is the whole reproducer.
 The CHECK-KEEP address memo was sized from the
 surviving binding count while the checker materializes a distinct
 type structure per mention, so on this unit the table saturated,
 the deep copy degraded to unmemoized, and the keep deck overflowed
 its floor into the check scratch it was still reading. The compiler
 died in a general-protection fault with no diagnostic of any kind,
 which is why this test exists: the crash was invisible to every
 harness that counts error lines. The loop below keeps the cited
 graph reachable so dead-code elimination cannot shrink the unit.

 We say:

Section: Probe

  loop-body-len : ShellCmd -> Integer
  loop-body-len (c) = when c
   is ScForLoop (name) (init) (cond) (step) (body) -> list-length body
   is otherwise -> 0 - 1

  opening : [Console] Nothing = act
    print-line-uni ("for-loop-body: " & show (loop-body-len (sh-for-loop "i" (SeInt 0) (SeInt 3) (SeInt 1) [sh-exit 0])))
    print-line-uni ("while-body: " & show (loop-body-len (sh-while (SeInt 1) [])))
  end
